{%- comment -%}
  The row above the grid — port of components/shop/results-toolbar.tsx.

  How many pieces are showing and what is narrowing them, then the sort control.

  Sort is the one facet that stays a form rather than becoming a set of links — a
  <select> is the right control for a handful of mutually exclusive orderings, and
  the design draws it that way. It is a plain GET, so it needs no JavaScript: the
  hidden fields carry the active filters through, and `page` is deliberately NOT
  among them, because a re-sorted catalogue starts again at page one.

  The orderings are Shopify's own `collection.sort_options` rather than the
  design's four hardcoded keys — which the merchant controls in admin, and which
  is the same reason the sort select exists at all.

  Accepts: collection, count, filter_label
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4 border-b border-hairline pb-4.5">
  <p class="text-caption text-ink-muted">
    <span data-numeric>{{ count }}</span> {{ 'catalogue.pieces' | t: count: count }} · {{ filter_label }}
  </p>

  <form action="{{ collection.url }}" method="get" class="flex items-center gap-3">
    {%- comment -%}
      Every applied facet is carried forward by hand. Without these the sort
      submit would silently clear the filters — and `page` is left out on
      purpose, so re-sorting lands on page one rather than page four of a
      different ordering.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- for filter in collection.filters -%}
      {%- for value in filter.active_values -%}
        <input type="hidden" name="{{ value.param_name }}" value="{{ value.value | escape }}">
      {%- endfor -%}
      {%- if filter.type == 'price_range' -%}
        {%- if filter.min_value.value -%}
          <input type="hidden" name="{{ filter.min_value.param_name }}" value="{{ filter.min_value.value }}">
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if filter.max_value.value -%}
          <input type="hidden" name="{{ filter.max_value.param_name }}" value="{{ filter.max_value.value }}">
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}

    <label for="sort" class="text-micro uppercase tracking-nav text-ink-subtle">{{ 'catalogue.sort' | t }}</label>
    <select
      id="sort"
      name="sort_by"
      class="min-h-11 cursor-pointer rounded-sm border border-line bg-canvas px-3.5 text-caption text-ink transition-colors duration-(--duration-base) focus:border-brand"
    >
      {%- assign current_sort = collection.sort_by | default: collection.default_sort_by -%}
      {%- for option in collection.sort_options -%}
        <option value="{{ option.value }}" {% if option.value == current_sort %}selected{% endif %}>{{ option.name }}</option>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </select>

    <button
      type="submit"
      class="inline-flex min-h-11 cursor-pointer items-center rounded-sm border border-line px-4 text-micro uppercase tracking-nav text-ink-muted transition-colors duration-(--duration-base) hover:border-brand hover:text-brand"
    >{{ 'catalogue.apply' | t }}</button>
  </form>
</div>
